    "readout_text": "To determine the value of \\( K \\), we recognize that for each positive integer \\( n \\leq 10 \\), the number of sequences \\( A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_n \\) where each \\( A_i \\) is a subset of \\( \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 10\\} \\) and \\( A_{i-1} \\subseteq A_i \\) is \\( (n+1)^{10} \\). Summing this over \\( n \\) from 1 to 10 gives:\n\n\\[\nK = \\sum_{n=1}^{10} (n+1)^{10} = \\sum_{m=2}^{11} m^{10}\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term modulo 10:\n\n- \\( 2^{10} \\equiv 24 \\mod 10 \\equiv 4 \\)\n- \\( 3^{10} \\equiv 59049 \\mod 10 \\equiv 9 \\)\n- \\( 4^{10} \\equiv 1048576 \\mod 10 \\equiv 6 \\)\n- \\( 5^{10} \\equiv 9765625 \\mod 10 \\equiv 5 \\)\n- \\( 6^{10} \\equiv 60466176 \\mod 10 \\equiv 6 \\)\n- \\( 7^{10} \\equiv 282475249 \\mod 10 \\equiv 9 \\)\n- \\( 8^{10} \\equiv 1073741824 \\mod 10 \\equiv 4 \\)\n- \\( 9^{10} \\equiv 3486784401 \\mod 10 \\equiv 1 \\)\n- \\( 10^{10} \\equiv 10000000000 \\mod 10 \\equiv 0 \\)\n- \\( 11^{10} \\equiv 25937424601 \\mod 10 \\equiv 1 \\)\n\nSumming these results:\n\n\\[\n4 + 9 + 6 + 5 + 6 + 9 + 4 + 1 + 0 + 1 = 45\n\\]\n\nFinally, \\( 45 \\mod 10 = 5 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
